   "text": {
    "L1": "Distance around a shape means the total length of its boundary.",
    "L2": "For a rectangle, we add all four sides.",
    "L3": "Opposite sides are equal, so the sides are 150, 100, 150 and 100 centimetres.",
    "L4": "Adding only 150 plus 100 misses two sides.",
    "L5": "Add the four sides: 150 plus 100 plus 150 plus 100.",
    "L6": "That gives 500 centimetres of lace around the tablecloth.",
    "L7": "Now place the total distance around the rectangle."
